# Docker build context is the REPO ROOT (see render.yaml: dockerContext: .).
# Without this file the context includes ~3.5 GB of local-only artifacts.

# Virtualenvs / node deps — reinstalled inside the image
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules

# Python bytecode & caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Next.js build output — the frontend is NOT part of the backend image
frontend/.next
frontend/out

# VCS & editor
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# Local runtime state — the Render Disk supplies these at /app/backend/data
backend/data
backend/datasets
backend/logs
*.log
**/mlruns

# Secrets — injected as Render env vars, never baked into the image
.env
**/.env

# Playwright storage_state files: live, session-hijackable account cookies.
# These are gitignored (so a Render build never sees them), but the build context
# is the local working tree — without this rule a local `docker build` copies real
# account sessions into an image layer, where they survive every later deletion.
#
# Sessions belong on the user's own machine (see the connector), never in an image.
**/.sessions
**/*storage_state.json

# Docs / assets not needed at runtime
*.pdf
DEPLOY.md
demo
